# The cusp at the reference resolution, both methods, same instrument.
# A = (z_c - z_min)/(z_max - z_c): a sphere gives 1; a trailing cusp stretches
# the lower half and A grows.  Integrated, so it has NO mesh floor.
# R/Req: radius of curvature at the lowest vertex, by a least-squares sphere
# through it and its ring, over the volume-equivalent radius.  LOCAL, so it DOES
# have a mesh floor -- see the last two rows, where both reach R ~ 1.07 h.
